res.status = 200, body = b'{"id":"chatcmpl-7d88f020e549facc52d12851debe69a5","created":1766037054,"model":"hosted_vllm/openai/gpt-oss-120b","object":"chat.completion","choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"content":"{Greedy construction starting from the ternary\xe2\x80\x91digit\xe2\x80\x91free Salem\xe2\x80\x93Spencer set and then iteratively adding shuffled remaining numbers while preserving the 3\xe2\x80\x91AP\xe2\x80\x91free property.}  \\n\\n```python\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\ndef heuristic(n, rng=None):\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    Construct a large 3\xe2\x80\x91AP\xe2\x80\x91free subset of {1,\xe2\x80\xa6,n} (n is expected to be 1094).\\n    The algorithm:\\n      1. Initialise with all numbers whose base\xe2\x80\x913 representation contains only 0 and 1.\\n      2. Shuffle the remaining candidates using a deterministic RNG derived from `rng`.\\n      3. Greedily insert each candidate if it does not create a three\xe2\x80\x91term arithmetic progression.\\n    Returns the set as a sorted list of integers.\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    # ---- initialise deterministic RNG ---------------------------------------\\n    if rng is None:\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\\n    elif isinstance(rng, (int, np.integer)):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(int(rng))\\n    elif isinstance(rng, np.random.Generator):\\n        # make a copy to avoid side\xe2\x80\x91effects\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(rng.integers(0, 2**63 - 1))\\n    else:\\n        raise TypeError(\\"rng must be None, int, or numpy.random.Generator\\")\\n\\n    # ---- helper to test whether adding x creates a 3\xe2\x80\x91AP --------------------\\n    def creates_ap(x, selected, size):\\n        \\"\\"\\"Return True if adding x to the current set `selected` would create an AP.\\"\\"\\"\\n        # selected is a bool array of length n+1 (index 0 unused)\\n        # iterate over existing elements a (where selected[a] is True)\\n        # Two checks:\\n        #   (i) x as middle: a + c = 2*x  -> c = 2*x - a\\n        #   (ii) x as endpoint: a + x = 2*mid  -> mid = (a + x)//2 when even\\n        for a in range(1, size + 1):\\n            if not selected[a]:\\n                continue\\n            # case (i): x is middle\\n            c = 2 * x - a\\n            if 1 <= c <= size and selected[c]:\\n                return True\\n            # case (ii): x is endpoint, look for middle element\\n            s = a + x\\n            if s % 2 == 0:\\n                mid = s // 2\\n                if selected[mid]:\\n                    return True\\n        return False\\n\\n    # ---- step 1: base\xe2\x80\x913 digit\xe2\x80\x91free set ---------------------------------------\\n    base_set = set()\\n    for num in range(1, n + 1):\\n        t = num\\n        ok = True\\n        while t:\\n            if t % 3 == 2:\\n                ok = False\\n                break\\n            t //= 3\\n        if ok:\\n            base_set.add(num)\\n\\n    # ---- bookkeeping arrays --------------------------------------------------\\n    selected = np.zeros(n + 1, dtype=bool)\\n    for v in base_set:\\n        selected[v] = True\\n\\n    # ---- step 2: shuffled remaining candidates --------------------------------\\n    remaining = [i for i in range(1, n + 1) if i not in base_set]\\n    rng.shuffle(remaining)\\n\\n    # ---- step 3: greedy insertion --------------------------------------------\\n    for cand in remaining:\\n        if not creates_ap(cand, selected, n):\\n            selected[cand] = True\\n\\n    # ---- return sorted list ---------------------------------------------------\\n    result = [i for i in range(1, n + 1) if selected[i]]\\n    return result\\n```","role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"We need to output code only? The user wants a description in braces then the implementation. Must be deterministic. Need heuristic to produce large Salem-Spencer set for n=1094. We can use known construction: base-3 representation, take numbers whose tern