e remaining list using gen.shuffle.\\n- For each x in list: if can_add(x) then present[x]=True.\\n- Return sorted list.\\n\\nOptionally do a local improvement: after addition pass, try to replace a present element with two absent that both can be added after removal. Could attempt limited iterations.\\n\\nBut we can skip.\\n\\nResult must be 3-AP-free; base-3 set is AP-free; adding only if doesn\'t create AP maintains property.\\n\\nWe\'ll implement can_add similar to earlier.\\n\\n Ensure determinism.\\n\\nReturn list.\\n\\nLet\'s craft answer.\\n\\n"}},"provider_specific_fields":{}}],"usage":{"completion_tokens":1329,"prompt_tokens":1650,"total_tokens":2979}}'
