res.status = 200, body = b'{"id":"chatcmpl-db46bf4b2e7d79a440f8caf9e6db926e","created":1766037109,"model":"hosted_vllm/openai/gpt-oss-120b","object":"chat.completion","choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"content":"{A deterministic greedy build that inserts numbers in increasing order of their \xe2\x80\x9cconflict score\xe2\x80\x9d (how many 3\xe2\x80\x91APs they could close), followed by a bounded single\xe2\x80\x91swap local improvement to replace a single conflicting element when it yields a net gain or equal size but opens later insertions.}  \\n\\n```python\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom typing import List, Union\\n\\ndef _make_rng(rng: Union[None, int, np.random.Generator]) -> np.random.Generator:\\n    \\"\\"\\"Return a NumPy Generator from various specifications.\\"\\"\\"\\n    if isinstance(rng, np.random.Generator):\\n        return rng\\n    if rng is None:\\n        rng = 0\\n    return np.random.default_rng(rng)\\n\\n\\ndef heuristic(n: int, rng=None) -> List[int]:\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    Construct a large 3\xe2\x80\x91AP\xe2\x80\x91free subset of {1,\xe2\x80\xa6,n} (n is expected to be 1094).\\n    The algorithm is deterministic for a given (n, rng) pair.\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    gen = _make_rng(rng)\\n\\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # 1.  Pre\xe2\x80\x91compute a cheap \xe2\x80\x9cconflict score\xe2\x80\x9d for each element:\\n    #    number of distinct triples (a,b,c) with a+b=2c that contain the element.\\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------\\n    score = np.zeros(n + 1, dtype=int)          # index 0 unused\\n    for a in range(1, n + 1):\\n        # b must be > a, c = (a+b)//2 integer \xe2\x86\x92 a+b even\\n        max_b = n\\n        for b in range(a + 1, max_b + 1):\\n            s = a + b\\n            if s & 1:          # odd \xe2\x86\x92 no integer middle\\n                continue\\n            c = s >> 1\\n            # the triple (a,c,b) contains a, c and b\\n            score[a] += 1\\n            score[b] += 1\\n            score[c] += 1\\n\\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # 2.  Order candidates by (score, random tie\xe2\x80\x91breaker) and greedy insert.\\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------\\n    candidates = list(range(1, n + 1))\\n    # random tie\xe2\x80\x91breaker \xe2\x80\x93 deterministic because we use the same rng each run\\n    gen.shuffle(candidates)\\n    # stable sort: primary key = score (ascending), secondary = original order\\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda x: score[x])\\n\\n    present = np.zeros(n + 1, dtype=bool)   # present[i] == True  \xe2\x87\x94 i \xe2\x88\x88 S\\n    S = []                                  # list version for fast iteration\\n\\n    def can_insert(x: int) -> bool:\\n        \\"\\"\\"True iff x can be added without creating a 3\xe2\x80\x91AP.\\"\\"\\"\\n        # check all y already in S\\n        for y in S:\\n            # x and y as endpoints \xe2\x86\x92 midpoint must not be present\\n            if ((x + y) & 1) == 0:\\n                mid = (x + y) >> 1\\n                if present[mid]:\\n                    return False\\n            # x as middle, y as an endpoint\\n            z = 2 * x - y\\n            if 1 <= z <= n and present[z]:\\n                return False\\n        return True\\n\\n    for x in candidates:\\n        if can_insert(x):\\n            present[x] = True\\n            S.append(x)\\n\\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # 3.  Single\xe2\x80\x91swap local improvement.\\n    #     Repeatedly try to replace a single element of S with a\\n    #     non\xe2\x80\x91selected element that conflicts with exactly one element.\\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------\\n    not_present = [v for v in range(1, n + 1) if not present[v]]\\n    gen.shuffle(not_present)\\n\\n    improved = True\\n    while improved:\\n        improved = False\\n        for x in not_present:\\n            # find elements of S that would break the AP\xe2\x80\x91free condition\\n            conflicting = []\\n            for y in S:\\n                # x with y as endpoints\\n                if ((x + y) & 1) == 0:\\n                    mid = (x + y) >> 1\\n                    if present[mid]:\\n                        conflicting.append(y)\\n                # x as middle, y as endpoint\\n                z = 2 * x - y\\n                if 1 <= z <= n and present[z]:\\n                    conflicting.append(y)\\n                # early abort if >1 conflict\\n                if len(conflicting) > 1:\\n                    break\\n            if len(conflicting) == 1:\\n                # perform the swap\\n                rem = conflicting[0]\\n                present[rem] = False\\n                S.remove(rem)\\n\\n                present[x] = True\\n                S.append(x)\\n\\n                not_present.remove(x)\\n                not_present.append(rem)\\n\\n                improved = True\\n                break   # restart scan after any change\\n\\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # 4.  Final greedy pass on the (now shuffled) leftovers \xe2\x80\x93 they may\\n    #     now fit after the swaps.\\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------\\n    leftovers = [v for v in range(1, n + 1) if not present[v]]\\n    gen.shuffle(leftovers)\\n    for x in leftovers:\\n        if can_insert(x):\\n            present[x] = True\\n            S.append(x)\\n\\n    # Return a sorted list for reproducibility\\n    S.sort()\\n    return S\\n```","role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"We must produce answer: description in braces, then Python code implementing heuristic with new algorithm different from provided. Must be deterministic given rng. Must aim to get largest set for n=1094. We need to actually compute a set perhaps known best s